{"id":"word:hebrew:H4116","type":"word","title":"מָהַר","subtitle":"H4116 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, to be liquid or flow easily, i.e. (by implication); to hurry (in a good or a bad sense); often used (with another verb) adverbially, promptly","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מָהַר (H4116) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 64 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מָהַר (mâhar) means properly, to be liquid or flow easily, i.e. (by implication); to hurry (in a good or a bad sense); often used (with another verb) adverbially, promptly First listed occurrence: 1Chr 12 9."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מָהַר","transliteration":"mâhar","pronunciation":"maw-har'","strong":"H4116","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4116","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יְמַהֵ֣ר","וַ/תְּמַהֵ֗ר","מִֽהֲר֖וּ","וַ/יְמַהֵ֖ר","לְ/מַהֵֽר"],"morphs":[["HC/Vpw3ms",9],["HC/Vpw3fs",8],["HC/Vpw3mp",6],["HVpv2ms",4],["HVpv2mp",4],["HR/Vpc",3],["HVpp3cp",3],["HVpv2ms/Sd",2],["HVpp3ms",2],["HVpi3ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, to be liquid or flow easily, i.e. (by implication); to hurry (in a good or a bad sense); often used (with another verb) adverbially, promptly","usage":"be carried headlong, fearful, (cause to make, in, make) haste(-n, -ily), (be) hasty, (fetch, make ready) × quickly, rash, × shortly, (be so) × soon, make speed, × speedily, × straightway, × suddenly, swift.","full":"H4116. mahar I. [ מָהַר ] verb hasten (Late Hebrew Pi`el,and derivatives; Arabic be practised, skilled (with Assyrian mâru , send , order , govern , compare II. מהר ); Ethiopic train teach ; Syriac Pa`el id. ; compare also Egyptian m¹har , trained warrior Bondi 57 ); — Niph`al Perfect 3feminine singular נִמְהָ֑רָה Job 5:13 ; Participle נִמְהָר Hab 1:6 ; plural נִמְהָרִים Isa 32:4 ; construct נִמְהֲרֵי 35:4 ; &#8212; be hurried = anxious, disturbed נְמְהֲרֵילֵֿב 35:4 ; hasty, precipitate , subject עֵצָה Job 5:13 ; so participle as substantive Isa 32:4 ; impetuous , of Chaldeans, Hab 1:6 (|| מַר ). Pi`el Perfect מִהַר 1Sam 4:14 ; Isa 51:14 ; 3 feminine singular מִהֲרָה Jer 48:16 etc.; Imperfect יְמַהֵר Isa 5:19 2 t.; וַיְמַהֵר Gen 18:6 8 t. (1 Sam 28:30 see below); 3 feminine plural תְּמַהֵרְנָה Jer 9:17 etc.; Imperative masculine singular מַהֵר Gen 19:22 +; מַהֲרָה 1Sam 23:27 ; 1Kin 22:9 , etc.; Infinitive construct מַהֵר Prov 7:23 +; Participle מְמַהֵר Gen 41:32 ; Mal 3:5 (on מַהֵר Zeph 1:14 [ 1Sam 23:22 ] compare Kö i. 268 Schw ZAW x. 1890, 176 see I. מַהֵר ), feminine plural מְמַהֲרוֺת Prov 6:18 ; &#8212; 1 hasten, make haste , = go or come quickly Gen 18:6 ; 1Sam 9:12 ( but strike out ᵐ5 We Dr Kit Bu HPS), Nahum 2:6 ; Isa 49:17 ; 1Chr 12:9 ; = go eagerly, (followed by Infinitive of purpose) Prov 1:16 ; Isa 59:7 ; Participle = swift, prompt Mal 3:5 ; of bird Prov 7:23 ; figurative of calamity Isa 5:19 (|| חוּשׁ ) Jer 48:16 , בַּז חָשׁ שָׁלָל מַהֵר Isa 8:1 , 3 , below 2 hasten + verb, ( ׳מ having really adverbial force): followed by Infinitive Gen 18:7 ( לַעֲשׂת מִהַר ); compare 27:20 ; 41:32 (subject God), Exod 2:18 ; 10:16 ; 12:33 ; 2Sam 15:14 ; Isa 32:4 ; 51:14 ; Prov 6:18 ; Eccl 5:1 ; more often followed by verb with ו Gen 24:18 , 20 , 46 ; 44:11 (all J), 45:9 , 13 (E), probably 43:30 (J), also Exod 34:8 (J), Josh 4:10 ; 8:14 , 19 (all J E), Judg 13:10 ; 1Sam 4:14 ; 17:48 ; 23:27 ; 25:18 , 23 , 34 (twice in verse); 28:24 ; 2Sam 15:14 ; 19:17 ; 1Kin 20:33 , 41 ; 2Kin 9:13 ; Jer 9:17 ; so even when active is not wholly voluntary 1Sam 28:20 (but read probably ᵐ5 וַיִּבָּהֵל We Dr Kit Bu); also, ו omitted, Psa 106:13 ; especially with Imperative Gen 19:22 (J), Judg 9:48 ; Est 6:10 ; so also עֲנֵנִי מַהֵר Psa 69:18 ; 102:3 ; 143:7 ; compare 79:8 (see Ol on the passage ). 3 transitive hasten , = prepare quickly Gen 18:6 ; = bring quickly 1Kin 22:9 2Chr 18:8 ; Est 5:5 ; = do quickly 2Chr 24:5 (twice in verse). I. מַהֵר adjective hastening, speedy, swift (strictly Pi`el Participle for מְמַהֵר see below מהר ); — of וּמ ׳קָרוֺב מְאד י, ׳יוֺם Zeph 1:14 ; read also feminine הַמְּהֵרָה ( רַגְלוֺ ) 1Sam 23:22 his swift foot (for ׳ר ׳מִ רָאָהוּ ᵑ0 ) Th We Dr Bu; deeper corruption assumed by HPS. II. מַהֵר adverb quickly, speedily (strictly Pi`el infinitive absolute ) always immediately after verb; Exod 32:8 (J), Deut 4:26 ; 7:4 , 22 ; 9:3 , 12 (twice in verse); 9:16 ; 28:20 ; Josh 2:5 (J), Judg 2:17 , 23 ; Prov 25:8 (on Psa 69:18 ; 79:8 ; 102:3 ; 143:7 , where ׳מ precedes, see above below מָהַר ).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 12 9","keyReferences":["1Chr 12 9","1Kgs 20 33","1Kgs 20 41","1Kgs 22 9","1Sam 4 14","1Sam 9 12","1Sam 17 48","1Sam 23 27"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":64,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 12 9","book":"1Chr","chapter":12,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/מַהֵֽר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vpc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 33","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":33,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יְמַהֲר֜וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 41","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":41,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יְמַהֵ֕ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 9","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מַהֲרָ֖/ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpv2ms/Sd"},{"reference":"1Sam 4 14","book":"1Sam","chapter":4,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִהַ֔ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpp3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 9 12","book":"1Sam","chapter":9,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מַהֵ֣ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpv2ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 17 48","book":"1Sam","chapter":17,"verse":48,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יְמַהֵ֣ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 23 27","book":"1Sam","chapter":23,"v